# Build context for the images that build musterd from source — deploy/cloud-seat/Dockerfile and
# scripts/perf/broadcast-bench.Dockerfile. Both are `COPY . .` from the repo root, so this file is
# the only thing standing between a developer's working tree and a published image layer.
#
# It wants the tree — but never the host's installed dependencies (wrong platform for
# better-sqlite3's native binding), never the history, and never per-seat state.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.vite
coverage
*.log

# Per-seat local state, none of it tracked in this repo (`git ls-tree origin/main .musterd` is
# empty — the durable roster of ADR 058 lives in the team home repo, not here). `.musterd/` holds
# the seat's binding, which carries a live credential at mode 600; a `COPY . .` from any seat
# worktree would bake that key into the image as a world-readable layer, which is the ADR 390
# least-privilege finding ("the hub's team agent key as a live Fly secret") one layer up.
#
# .gitignore already keeps these out of commits, file by file. Docker does not read .gitignore, so
# the same protection has to be stated here — and here it is stated as the whole directory, since
# nothing under it belongs in an image at all.
.musterd/
**/.musterd/

# Harness-provisioned, per-workspace and personal, written by `musterd init` / the harness itself
# (ADR 085). Same class: not tracked, not wanted in an image, and `.codex/` can hold auth.
.claude/
**/.claude/
.codex/
**/.codex/
